The journal is wanted — and the part you wanted most already exists

> I do think I want the journal engine.

Reverses the *not wanted* row in `docs/ADVOCATE.md` §6. The refusal was about
**publishing** — FCPM has its own ways — and this is about the root page having a
**provider**. Different jobs, so the row says what changed rather than being
quietly rewritten.

**First move recorded as you framed it:** `/journal` on `main`, prefixes stay,
*"journal can power what we've done. It's just that journal can do more."*

## Two blogs on one repository is not a feature request

You described wanting the library treatment — journal content from a branch
rather than a prefix, so two split-identity machines get their separateness
without becoming two repositories. **The journal engine already works exactly
that way.** From its own orientation:

> It is per-branch content. One repository serving several places branches per
> destination and each branch carries its own `NAME`, so **the number of branches
> is the number of nodes** — disclosed rather than inferred.

A branch with its own `/NAME` and its own `journal/` *is* a second node
publishing from one repository. So I did not file a petition: it would be asking
for shipped behaviour, which is the exact waste the petition ground exists to
prevent.

What is left is yours, and I have written it down rather than answered it:
**what the second branch is for.** Per bay is the obvious reading of *split
identity* and it is not obviously right — two bays are two machines, not two
voices, and the journal's unit is a destination rather than a host.

## The finding worth having before you mount it

**`.journal-engine` has to go in `site/`, not at the node root.**

The engine is referenced as a path *inside* the mounting site — its own config
excludes `.journal-engine/` from the build, which only makes sense if it sits in
the source tree. Jekyll cannot reach outside `source:`, the same wall
`site/_data` hits. So after #86:

| | where | because |
|---|---|---|
| `.advocate-engine` | the node root | it **runs**. Nothing in the build reads it |
| `.journal-engine` | **`site/`** | the **build reads it** — layouts, includes, plugins |

Mounting it beside the advocate engine would look consistent and would not work.

Also flagged for that pull request rather than after it: `journal/` content would
live at `site/journal/`, and this repository has a documented history of
Cloudflare reporting it **damaged** when a submodule could not resolve under a
shallow clone — the unconfirmed hypothesis in `deploying.md` names
`.advocate-engine` for precisely that.

**Nothing is mounted here.** That is still your pull request.
